why Every Horde quest of Blackrock Depths, with the second run Thrall's chain needs.

# Blackrock Depths' Horde quests in one guide: Mulgore, the Undercity, Kargath
# in the Badlands, Blackrock Mountain's quarry, the Burning Steppes, a first
# run, the hand-ins with Thrall in Orgrimmar and The Love Potion's errands in
# Azshara and Un'Goro Crater, a second run, then the last hand-ins and Grark
# Lorkrub. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up wherever
# the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - Thunderheart's 3906 Disharmony of Flame -> 3907 Disharmony of Fire;
#   Galamav the Marksman's 3981 Commander Gor'shak -> Gor'shak's 3982 -> 4001
#   What Is Going On? -> Thrall's 4002 The Eastern Kingdom -> 4003 The Royal
#   Rescue (the second run: the Emperor) -> Princess Moira's 4004 The
#   Princess Saved?; Vivian Lagrave's 7201 The Last Element.
# - Apothecary Zinge's 4133 Vivian Lagrave -> 4134 Lost Thunderbrew Recipe.
# - The WANTED poster's 4081 KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves -> the second
#   poster's 4082 (its kills in the second run) -> Lexlort's 4122 Grark
#   Lorkrub -> 4121 Precarious Predicament.
# - Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania's 4061 -> 4062 -> Lotwil Veriatus' 4063 The
#   Rise of the Machines.
# - Alaana Stormwalker's 97197 Fragment of the Firelands; Maxwort Uberglint's
#   4123 The Heart of the Mountain; Cyrus Therepentous' 4023 -> 4024 A Taste of
#   Flame; Franclorn Forgewright's 3801 -> 3802 Dark Iron Legacy (the
#   Shadowforge Key); Yuka Screwspigot's 4136 Ribbly Screwspigot.
# - Mistress Nagmara's 4201 The Love Potion (taken inside, handed in on the
#   second run).
#
# Left out: 4132 Operation: Death to Angerforge (it opens only after the
# second run's kills, so it would need a third run); 4295 Rocknot's Ale
# (repeatable); 4083 The Spectral Chalice (it needs the Mining skill); 3911,
# the giverless The Last Element; 7604 A Binding Contract (it needs Molten
# Core); 8961 Three Kings of Flame and 9015 The Challenge (the Dungeon Set 2
# and Valthalak chains); the breadcrumb 4324 Yuka Screwspigot from Tanaris
# (off this guide's way; Ribbly opens without it); 4022 and the Searing Gorge
# chain before it (4023, the other A Taste of Flame, opens 4024 without
# them); the Thorium Brotherhood's favours (repeatable).
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Commander Gor'shak, Kharan,
# Mistress Nagmara, Princess Moira or the Monument of Franclorn Forgewright
# inside, so their goals stand at the door (@34.8,85.3, Searing Gorge) with
# `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal,
# not of a recorded run; every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a
# group that takes them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The Heart of the Mountain's quest needs a
#   Relic Coffer Key, which the Anvilrage dwarves drop; the data names no
#   source for the Heart itself. Cyrus's Frenzied Black Drake drops the
#   Black Dragonflight Molt. The quest texts place Pyron in the quarry, Kharan
#   in a cell near Gor'shak, and Grark's escort through Blackrock Mountain.
#   Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards from the Anvilrage
#   Wardens and the essences' sources outside (in the Searing Gorge); those
#   goals stay at the door for the ones inside.
# - The door: QuestieDB's list of Forever's dungeons, as Polestar's Codex holds it
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   52 to 60).
# INGAME: where inside do Commander Gor'shak, Kharan, Mistress Nagmara, the
#   Monument and the Heart of the Mountain stand?

